---
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Rhyss Vivian: enterprise infrastructure, cybersecurity, platform direction, and leadership.">
  <section class="border-b theme-border theme-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:py-20">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] theme-eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-normal theme-text sm:text-5xl">
        I am a technology leader with a technical foundation, growing toward broader platform and executive scope.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 theme-muted">
        My background is rooted in enterprise infrastructure: the operational systems, identity
        platforms, network changes, security controls, and governance work that organizations depend on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:py-20">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Leadership shape"
      title="The work sits between technical reality and organizational direction."
      description="I am most interested in roles where platform, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and leadership are not separate conversations."
    />
    <div class="space-y-6 leading-8 theme-muted">
      <p>
        I have spent a lot of time in traditional enterprise infrastructure, where strong outcomes
        require more than tool familiarity. They require change management, communication, timing,
        vendor coordination, risk judgment, and steady execution under operational constraints.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am now spending more time building: moving a homelab toward Infrastructure as Code,
        pushing more configuration into versioned workflows, and sharpening the software/platform
        side of my skill set without pretending my background is something it is not.
      </p>
      <p>
        This fall, I begin MBA work that will add more structure to the business side of the same
        arc: how technology strategy, security, operations, and leadership decisions compound.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:py-20">
      <SectionHeading
        eyebrow="Direction"
        title="Senior technology leadership, with hands still on the systems."
        description="The long-term direction is CIO/CTO-level work: setting technology direction with enough technical context to know where the hard parts are."
      />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 p-5">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-normal">Platform</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
            Repeatable systems, operational leverage, automation, and practical standards.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 p-5">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-normal">Security</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
            IAM, compliance readiness, control implementation, and risk-aware infrastructure.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 p-5">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-normal">Leadership</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
            Clear priorities, accountable execution, and translation between business and technical teams.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
